.TH compbench 1 "November 2026" "compbench 2.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
compbench \- benchmark Btrfs transparent compression
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B compbench
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIDEVICE\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B compbench
benchmarks Btrfs compression algorithms (zstd, lzo, zlib) and no
compression by measuring write throughput, read throughput, compression
ratio, CPU usage, and physical disk I/O.
.PP
All metrics are gathered through direct kernel interfaces with no text
parsing of external tool output:
.IP \(bu 2
write/read timing via
.BR clock_gettime (2)
.RI ( CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW );
.IP \(bu 2
compression ratio via
.BR statvfs (2);
.IP \(bu 2
CPU usage via
.IR /proc/stat ;
.IP \(bu 2
physical disk I/O via
.IR /sys/block/*/stat ;
.IP \(bu 2
data copy via
.BR copy_file_range (2).
.PP
.SH WARNING
.B This tool erases all data on DEVICE.
It creates a fresh Btrfs filesystem on each test run. Double-check the
device path before proceeding. Before anything is written, compbench
prints the disk model and size and asks for confirmation (type
.BR yes ).
.SH "DISK STATE AFTER A RUN"
The device is not restored after a run. Without
.BR \-\-hdd ,
DEVICE is left containing the Btrfs filesystem of the last test. With
.BR \-\-hdd ,
DEVICE is left with a GPT partition table and two partitions, each
containing the Btrfs filesystem of its last test. The previous contents
cannot be recovered.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B DEVICE
Block device to test (e.g.
.IR /dev/sdX ).
.TP
.B ARCHIVE
Local path or URL to a
.I .tar.xz
archive used as the test dataset.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-repeat = N
Repeat each test
.I N
times and average the results (default: 1). When
.I N
> 1, the standard deviation of the write and read throughput is also
reported in the CSV output. The total number of tests (levels ×
algorithms × variants × zones × repeats) may not exceed 4096.
.TP
.BR \-\-zstd = MIN\-MAX
zstd compression level range
.RI ( \-15..\-1 or 1..15 ,
default:
.IR 1\-15 ).
Negative levels are available since kernel 6.15. A single level may be
given instead of a range (e.g.
.IR \-\-zstd\ 5 ).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force = MODE
Force mode controls
.B compress-force
versus standard
.B compress
mount behaviour. One of:
.RS
.TP 12
.B none
standard
.B compress=
for all tests (default);
.TP
.B zstd
.B compress-force=
for zstd, standard for others;
.TP
.B lzo
.B compress-force=
for lzo, standard for others;
.TP
.B all
.B compress-force=
for all algorithms;
.TP
.B both
run each test twice (standard and force) and print a side-by-side
comparison table.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-\-hdd = PERCENT
Partition the device and test on the first and last
.I PERCENT
of the disk (1\-50), to evaluate spatial performance variation (typical
for spinning disks). An interpolated average across both zones is also
reported.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output = FILE
Export results to
.I FILE
in CSV format with full run metadata.
.TP
.B \-\-no-integrity-check
Skip the
.B xz
archive integrity check.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
The results table reports, per target:
.TP 12
.B WrMiB/s
synced write throughput (copy + sync);
.TP
.B RdMiB/s
read throughput after a page-cache clear (cold read);
.TP
.B WrDisk*
actual bytes written to physical media;
.TP
.B RdDisk*
actual bytes read from physical media;
.TP
.B Ratio
space consumed divided by uncompressed data size;
.TP
.B WrCPU% \ / \ RdCPU%
system CPU usage during write/read;
.TP
.B Sec/Red
seconds per 1% space reduction (speed/compression balance; lower is
better).
.PP
A
.I "Best Results"
summary highlights the fastest write, fastest read, best compressed, and
best balanced target per disk zone.
.SH NOTES
For accurate results:
.IP \(bu 2
.I WrCPU% \ / \ RdCPU%
are system-wide
.I /proc/stat
figures covering all processes; run compbench on an otherwise idle
machine.
.IP \(bu 2
.I Ratio
is derived from
.BR statvfs (2)
free space. Btrfs allocates space in chunks, so small datasets can
show quantized ratios; use a dataset that is large relative to the
test filesystem.
.IP \(bu 2
.B sync()
is system-wide: synced write timings include writeback of unrelated
dirty data on the machine.
.IP \(bu 2
Cold reads require a writable
.IR /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches .
When the page cache cannot be dropped (e.g. inside some containers),
.I RdMiB/s
is inflated; a warning is printed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
all requested tests completed and succeeded;
.TP
.B 1
error (invalid arguments, missing privileges, user abort, interruption,
or a failed operation), or at least one benchmark test failed. Failed
tests are excluded from the results and a warning reports how many; if
every test fails, no results are produced.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic run:
.B compbench /dev/sdX https://example.com/archive.tar.xz
.TP
Repeated, zstd 1\-10, both force modes, HDD zones:
.B compbench /dev/sdX archive.tar.xz \-n 3 \-\-zstd 1\-10 \-f both \-\-hdd 10 \-v
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Must be run as root. Requires
.BR btrfs-progs ,
.BR xz-utils ,
.BR gdisk ,
and
.B curl
(on PATH) when fetching a remote archive.
.SH FILES
CSV output is written to the path given by
.BR \-\-output .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfs.btrfs (8),
.BR mount (8),
.BR btrfs (5)
